game (
	name "A Crimson Spring"
	description "From Baf's Guide: A thoroughly dark superhero game--you're a superhero out to avenge your girlfriend's (gruesome and minutely described) death. The multimedia aspect is good (the sound is better than the graphics), the writing's strong, and the plot is fairly complex--and the PC is nicely rendered as well; this is no stock jut-jawed invincible superhero. There are some implementation problems, though--at one point, SEARCH ROOM is a required command), and some of the event triggers are easy to miss. Plenty of sex and violence here, so this is not for the faint of heart."
	releaseyear "1900"
	releasemonth "1"
	releaseday "1"
	developer "Rob Sherwin"
	genre "Adventure / Interactive Fiction"
	users "1"
	publisher "Freeware"
	code "acs"
